 "key_results": {
  "T1": "For one fixed future null k=E(1,-n), |n|=1, observers e0 and fourVelocity(beta) with |beta|<1: E_old=E, E_new=gamma(1+beta.n)E, D=E_new/E_old>0 independent of E; new-frame components Binv k describe the same vector (Bst*Binv k=k); measured energy invariant under the passive frame change; new sourceward direction = aberr (unit, onto the sphere); D*gamma(1-beta.n')=1.",
  "T2": "Polar chart with axis beta-hat: d mu'/d mu = D^-2 (HasDerivAt), mu'=(mu+b)/(1+b mu) a bijection of [-1,1] with endpoints fixed; for every g continuous on [-1,1], int g(mu'(mu)) D^-2 dmu = int g dmu' and the dphi-iterated version; total solid angle 4 pi; chart_link proves the general-beta closed form has polar cosine mu' and unchanged azimuth; d_A=sqrt(dS/dOmega) with the same dS gives d_A'=D d_A.",
  "T3": "endpoint_optical_same_ray: z'=zNew z D, d_A'=dANew d_A D and (1+z')d_A'=(1+z)d_A for the same ray, 0<|beta|<1.",
  "T4": "With reciprocity d_L=(1+z)^2 d_A assumed in each frame: d_L'=d_L/D (=dLNew), d_L/(1+z) invariant.",
  "T5": "Planck occupation invariance (hypothesis) gives T'=D T0 and 1/T'=a+b.n' with a=gamma/T0, b=-gamma beta/T0, a^2-|b|^2=1/T0^2; inversion beta=-b/a, gamma(-b/a)/a=1/sqrt(a^2-|b|^2) (matches inverse_temperature_boost); iff-criterion (TBO-07) proved.",
  "boundaries": "beta=0: D=1, identity frame change, n'=n, mu'=mu, Jacobian 1, z'=z, d_A'=d_A, d_L'=d_L, T'=T0; z=0: (1+zNew 0 D) dANew dA D = dA.",
  "negative_control": "Same ray, different observers: energies 1 vs 2; mixing Doppler factors of two distinct rays (D=2 vs 1/2) gives product 4 != 1. Non-vacuity: beta=(0,0,3/5), n=(0,0,1) satisfies all composite hypotheses with D=2."
 },
